    heading: "Our Abu Dhabi starting prices, and the lines that sit outside them",
    note: `A static site of up to 100 pages starts from ${P.site}, an SEO or catalogue site of 299 pages or more from ${P.seoSite}, an online store from ${P.shop}, and a portal or supplier tool from ${P.software}. Monthly search work starts from ${P.seo} and upkeep from ${P.care} once the two free months after launch have run. Inside those figures: design, build, bilingual layout engineering and right-to-left testing, real-device testing, structured data, analytics, launch and a documented handover. Outside them, and paid to their own suppliers rather than to us, are the lines that dominate an Abu Dhabi budget: Arabic translation priced by word, legal or certified translation where a document requires it, photography anywhere in the emirate, domain and hosting, in-country hosting if a client's policy demands it, certification and audit fees for your document pack, and any attestation or notarisation. We quote in USD because we invoice from India, and the dirham's peg to the dollar keeps the converted figure stable between approval and payment. Nothing is billed before you approve the itemised quote in writing.`,
